Source: sekisho
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Naoto Morishima <naoto256@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cargo, rustc (>= 1.95)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/naoto256/sekisho

Package: sekishod
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Description: Identity-Aware Proxy daemon (sekishod)
 Rust-based identity-aware proxy with OIDC/SAML authentication,
 ACME TLS certificate management, and policy-based access control.
 .
 This package contains the proxy daemon (sekishod), its systemd unit,
 the /etc/default/sekishod environment file, and the system user the
 service runs as. Operators install sekisho-cli alongside this package
 to manage the daemon, and sekisho-webui for a browser-based admin UI.

Package: sekisho-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, sekishod (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Sekisho management CLI (sekisho-cli)
 JunOS-style interactive shell for managing a sekishod daemon over its
 local control socket. Version-locked to sekishod: a sekisho-cli binary
 only talks to a daemon of the exact same version, so this package
 strictly depends on the matching sekishod package.

Package: sekisho-webui
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, sekishod (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Sekisho web admin UI (sekisho-webui)
 Read/write web admin UI (axum + Maud + HTMX) for the sekishod
 management API. Ships its own systemd unit, disabled by default —
 operators opt in per host. Version-locked to sekishod, so this
 package strictly depends on the matching sekishod package.
